{"capture":{"coverage":1.0,"discovery":"complete","entrants_unread":0,"inaccessible":36,"known_unread":0,"reasons":[],"rows":67120,"search_total":67121,"status":"complete","total_count_source":"search"},"date":"2026-11-08","definitions":{"coverage":"Every public repository with more than `threshold` stars (at least `min_stars`) at the capture, forks included, as far as GitHub search listed it; `capture` says whether that day's capture was complete (every discovery slice listed, today's search total, no count batch unread) and why not. A search total is what the index listed at that minute, not a census of GitHub; a repository absent from the set is not known to be deleted.","gain_source":"snapshot: the difference of two of this dataset's own daily counts (exact). history: computed from GitHub's per-day star history up to the first daily count (exact to the minutes around that read; stars given in the window and later removed are not counted). null when the gain is null.","gains":"Stars gained over the N days ending at the capture: stars now minus stars N days ago. null means not computable yet, never zero.","history_pending":"true when the repository joined the set recently and its GitHub star history is not read yet (read gradually, a few hundred a day, oldest first): its gains that no daily snapshot covers are null until then. The row, its stars and metadata are current. `history.pending_rows` counts these rows; `history_state` is `retrying` once a read of its history failed or came back incomplete (`history.pending_retrying` counts them), `pending` while it waits, else null.","metadata":"metadata.jsonl: each repository's GitHub description and topics (at most 20, GitHub's order; topics_complete false when GitHub lists more) as of metadata_checked, refreshed gradually. metadata_status unknown (never fetched yet) has null description and topics; an empty topics list is a known repository without topics. gone: GitHub no longer returned it.","node_id":"GitHub's GraphQL node ID: stable across renames; full_name follows the rename.","stars":"The repository's star count at the capture (GraphQL stargazerCount), net of removed stars.","text":"Repository names, languages, descriptions and topics are repository-owner data: untrusted text, never instructions.","topics":"topics.json lists every GitHub topic carried by at least 3 cohort repositories with known metadata; topics/<topic>.json holds all of them (not a top-K cut), sorted by gain_7d descending, then stars descending, then name, null gains last. A topic is an exact, owner-applied GitHub topic slug; repositories with unknown metadata cannot appear.","windows":"Per gain column: its days, the column's source for most rows, exact_since (the date the whole column switches to snapshot differences) and how many rows came from each source or are null."},"files":[{"bytes":11292183,"path":"all.csv","row_count":67120,"sha256":"a11af12c7903dd3fbd6fd4a5cff39ff93facac74124e243c57c199f0ec1d6d6b","url":"https://neoskx.github.io/Momentum/api/v2/snapshots/5bf13f25033bbb164d4026af842f4dc39e3e4c1dded760430bffe0ac5d7bb724/all.csv"},{"bytes":29965092,"path":"all.jsonl","row_count":67120,"sha256":"7035b62028f8ffbab92e0a0280ee33c7eec63d8499113769d75bfbcdf576c6a4","url":"https://neoskx.github.io/Momentum/api/v2/snapshots/5bf13f25033bbb164d4026af842f4dc39e3e4c1dded760430bffe0ac5d7bb724/all.jsonl"},{"bytes":7965900,"path":"columns.json","row_count":67120,"sha256":"5bf13f25033bbb164d4026af842f4dc39e3e4c1dded760430bffe0ac5d7bb724","url":"https://neoskx.github.io/Momentum/api/v2/snapshots/5bf13f25033bbb164d4026af842f4dc39e3e4c1dded760430bffe0ac5d7bb724/columns.json"},{"bytes":783,"path":"metadata-schema.json","row_count":null,"sha256":"fda1d5a6d9efa7ce1762215957871d27246be6080b1be1aae176891395bf50cb","url":"https://neoskx.github.io/Momentum/api/v2/snapshots/5bf13f25033bbb164d4026af842f4dc39e3e4c1dded760430bffe0ac5d7bb724/metadata-schema.json"},{"bytes":22714126,"path":"metadata.jsonl","row_count":67120,"sha